,3,937,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA regular tetrahedron is a pyramid with four faces, each of which is an equilateral triangle.\n\nLet $ABCD$ be a regular tetrahedron and let $P$ be the unique point equidistant from points $A,B,C,D$. Extend $\\overrightarrow{AP}$ to hit face $BCD$ at point $Q$. What is the ratio $PQ/AQ$ ?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"79500257828157cbaa3a7c4a2028cb8b7ed769aca498dd4f36309942a8d93284"},"seconds":22.87346601486206,"seed":749496815244231859,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we first need to understand the geometric properties of a regular tetrahedron and how the point \\(P\\) (the centroid of the tetrahedron) relates to the vertices and the faces.\n\n1. **Identify the centroid \\(P\\):**\n   The centroid \\(P\\) of a regular tetrahedron is the point equidistant from all four vertices \\(A, B, C,\\) and \\(D\\). This point is also the center of mass of the tetrahedron.\n\n2. **Position of \\(Q\\):**\n   When we extend the line segment \\(\\overrightarrow{AP}\\) to intersect the face \\(BCD\\) at point \\(Q\\), we need to determine the ratio \\(PQ/AQ\\).\n\n3. **Use symmetry and properties of centroids:**\n   The centroid \\(P\\) divides each median of the tetrahedron in the ratio 3:1, where the longer part is closer to the vertex. This means that if we consider the median from \\(A\\) to the centroid of the face \\(BCD\\), the centroid \\(P\\) of the tetrahedron will divide this median in the ratio 3:1.\n\n4. **Determine the ratio \\(PQ/AQ\\):**\n   Since \\(P\\) divides the median in the ratio 3:1, and \\(Q\\) is the point where the line \\(AP\\) intersects the face \\(BCD\\), the segment \\(AQ\\) is divided by \\(P\\) in the ratio 3:1. Therefore, \\(PQ\\) is 1/4 of \\(AQ\\).\n\nSo, the ratio \\(PQ/AQ\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
